[{"id":"VRCE-5-37-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":1,"english":"Having made over the gem, Sītā said to Hanumān, This sign is very well known to Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f793058c4f1e8161418667158528616153407b61e25dbbf645a52cd3afcab9ea","compact":"53a46253712503a4584afb2bb4989585f5bd27aff4fded35410aab74e526bf1c","nasal":"3b622f935cd1e8533480b64ae90b81d463d90a5ee976f3b1286e61330add4f11"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":2,"english":"Seeing this gem, that hero, Rāma, shall recollect three persons, his mother, myself, and king Dasaratha, You, O foremost of monkeys, will again be commissioned on this business.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.783,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"750d819badd793e425d761844df09fae8ad28096e1cdb6b39b81222ff50c33c4","compact":"89ce2cfaf9a68f8dbc196df3057a3d2b04676137b73b6337c25d5d669571993f","nasal":"89ce2cfaf9a68f8dbc196df3057a3d2b04676137b73b6337c25d5d669571993f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":3,"english":"Do you bethink you as to what you will do afterwards, when you had been entrusted with this task.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea7f6d233e7ce95b4b30c4b147a2cf0d4db01476a340ead03007bd2434c03fdb","compact":"1d488f89ec8f1c5a990fb7bb66c6df606aff52087c9c7423e175819e55ea9ffe","nasal":"93ace73c1923c4ff5f05302650cddb36c5c63a670ce3f695762961fe931732bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":4,"english":"O foremost of monkeys, you are capable of compassing this work. Therefore, think as to what course of his (Rāma's) shall remove (my) misery.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84ce3b6595a7e3c64d8010e902d84bbd6771c538321bbdbf4ecc1abfa606dca5","compact":"de95e60a7958751821ff3d69cdd43c49433caea83346f0902a216e6c51edbb27","nasal":"c06a07ef153fe1d1dbb5c7bcca81e39e14ca2f56c85bcb2991db649c67371bb6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":5,"english":"O Hanumān, undergoing toils, be you instrumental in removing my misery. Saying, \"So be it,” the Wind-god's offspring of terrible prowess, bowing down the head, prepared to depart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65161d1f5be6cfbd7e26e3170e6e1e3058249ea252180bd43381ed7d50917aca","compact":"2184a1f7a60b015c31e8911a8c06b34ce72eb3b31131711328cacb7a95cd608e","nasal":"06f209cd3e8e03233856df8f7141b7225f83921c9d971753853ddcf718eca1a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":6,"english":"Seeing that (Hanumān) was about to set out, that exalted one, Mithila's daughter, addressed that monkey, son to the Wind-god, in words choked by the vapour of grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.706,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c01156d741cb6641edd937f70e2e61a97952fc56710efcada056e4b8a3001442","compact":"8955a397ebb28e52725b793d99a7cf7151519f9de9ef3d741dcfc2fd5ad5f6a1","nasal":"416ef8c4be9c9fea736e27e6f7ae86d0cbb6bb2a8dafff03ede589c940e11d42"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":7,"english":"O Hanumān, do you communicate good news to both Rāma and Lakşmaņa, to Sugrīva with his counsellors, and to all the aged monkeys. And, O best of monkeys, in consonance with righteousness, communicate good tidings (to Rāma).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.478,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e443984fe29814889e0d19118a2129c1173c52092f9bb21cce78bf49d5ef954","compact":"257f6fc347e9c59507c65970e50b17d0bc614c05e8fe15768899dbc7d8b864c5","nasal":"257f6fc347e9c59507c65970e50b17d0bc614c05e8fe15768899dbc7d8b864c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":8,"english":"And it behove you so to compass things that the mighty-armed Rāghava may rescue me from this sea of sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b3aeffa64b9c229d1b1601d250e8b2db6feb00cb30477b3ca3b20dfc0b88b17","compact":"6644c0050a57d8e4610399f66c756af80faee49134b79b19dadea25dba6c5725","nasal":"bcdbed1390f0680a65fdccbf211b387deb27d32312e1639c8945b92a2a3185f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":9,"english":"O Hanumān, do you speak so that the illustrious Rāma may deliver me while I am still alive; and thereby do you reap righteousness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf2a8b47d8ea08dde38bc64fedfd1bcf650e282b6b4750bed2b1a0ab940155ac","compact":"d9ca85a7b55d601b39bc74a4e39b06b2eaa939a8ce060b6bd4295266f61659fb","nasal":"c06a6d718e6904dcf63298388d8748dbdda94315cc61166c3bb8920b80c09742"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":10,"english":"Ever breathing high spirits, Dasarathi, (Dasaratha's son) hearing my words, shall attain an access of manliness for my deliverance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"17024f52088eb4c6ab7d8709ad086e393ef19fedeb0952e275a120705a037163","compact":"16590f4807fb14eecec9f6ca1716e202c8b8585271df47325db8bf6cf0d6b0b1","nasal":"16590f4807fb14eecec9f6ca1716e202c8b8585271df47325db8bf6cf0d6b0b1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":11,"english":"Soon as Rāghava shall hear words couching tidings of me, that hero shall duly resolve on displaying his prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c5f1c42f578287da4cac894eb0f0221a1700bb7aa7b190b855fceea279a49b34","compact":"4783cee9bfa9d6eebca8e70712817d6b93572c0fd97506d906d4155060fa4744","nasal":"4783cee9bfa9d6eebca8e70712817d6b93572c0fd97506d906d4155060fa4744"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":12,"english":"Hearing this speech of Sītā, Hanumān, son to the Wind-good, with his joined hands raised to his head, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3dce992c17fd2a1a8d9f60f0cfe20d1f69abd84e9846c7c69ba5cb06fc3ef835","compact":"3d67fa5bcf7b5345141c5530e3e87457a05db612ae5786dcda497d5fb61ab3e2","nasal":"70dba811b0d81574d85b034dbf666948b70e9b14a65631bd572b4da8b0ba3eed"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":13,"english":"Soon shall Käkutstha come, surrounded by the foremost monkeys and bears; and, vanquishing the foe in fight, shall remove your grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.743,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9902c171e10c7e8c711b289511c591876c97e03a205ea8c243dbeab8b5ce1dc7","compact":"e6f90414112e18db8322091c2b5b6f239f6da2891357443156d8a863d663d9cf","nasal":"e6f90414112e18db8322091c2b5b6f239f6da2891357443156d8a863d663d9cf"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":14,"english":"Find I none either among men, or Asuras, or celestials, that dares remain before him as he discharges his shafts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.641,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"80034cd45731d1136b99359bbf87d11679f724f2c6c46e5875be2fca7cc65817","compact":"0db1cd7fd20ff3d23b408c8ffe2b5bb026c68eaf9413886d37491863610e9967","nasal":"0db1cd7fd20ff3d23b408c8ffe2b5bb026c68eaf9413886d37491863610e9967"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":15,"english":"For you, in especial, he can stand in conflict even the Sun, Indra, nay-Yama himself, that offspring of the Sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"69a369a5701b83b3ef61dba7e340bdbf6447e6f4a4065d1283ea83b0d0a0edff","compact":"a22f484446066f1c1352c949e9e4c35420fde29d354430c5e6f46ae334571bfa","nasal":"a22f484446066f1c1352c949e9e4c35420fde29d354430c5e6f46ae334571bfa"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":16,"english":"For you, he prepare himself to conquer the Earth bounded by the main; and victory, you daughter of Janaka, shall be Rāma's.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.603,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"64a34a18874aeacd84acad0debb8e0b08f00213c3974c71e04f3efc457a9a1b6","compact":"d860ded7b5d4d3bc9af65cfb5a247134d7ba7f2a30c01a4e5b1471df050884fb","nasal":"87203463d97d6d5a7f848e6e40ded05993a6d3be056c2b239fb7af37093fde54"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":17,"english":"Hearing his words excellently spoken and thoroughly true, Jānaki honoured them highly, and spoke (as follows).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec6d3f04b61e4ba614728d6e76f6857c5bf1c3d2b895ac565da695ea511ad8ae","compact":"cec446c5062c139a5b476f292d6639e4666fbb76b10b8daf8e18b58045767214","nasal":"cec446c5062c139a5b476f292d6639e4666fbb76b10b8daf8e18b58045767214"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":18,"english":"And gazing at him once and again as he prepared to go away, Sītā froin affection honoured the speech which had been uttered (by Hanuman) out of attachment to his master.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2becba4145edcef9709bb53e3fef2b4f02d9f52ae5fd51bc7914562e4c37b3bb","compact":"129280c67aa8c97f2ab1fe523fa2d023b0b5c6bce87e084af663ba6956315f35","nasal":"129280c67aa8c97f2ab1fe523fa2d023b0b5c6bce87e084af663ba6956315f35"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":19,"english":"If you wish it, O hero, do you, O subduer of enemies, stay here for one day. Having rested in some hidden nook, you will depart tomorrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f0a6de4db8fa63d85bea35147a4c4cf9eaf4c19e98f4e9c35ed872e5e9ec6516","compact":"b87109ccc8196f646845c9a545bc823b68bc897a34620cc1a1a9246646572d41","nasal":"02dfe6391822589f2e20fecb14856b49c09c7652030028e45419656505ad8a0d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":20,"english":"O monkey, (if you do remain), your vicinity shall for a moment remove the huge grief of me of slender luck.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.448,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb6ad10dbe529ab8e678cecb24c7b404b0d70aa72c0d74201cfb80645bbbd659","compact":"6d97d19ec6ba40618ba787d87ccf3937718c2cfa08b3fcb9db95aa9f17b694e8","nasal":"6d97d19ec6ba40618ba787d87ccf3937718c2cfa08b3fcb9db95aa9f17b694e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":21,"english":"But even if you go (passing today here), I have, O tiger-like monkey, doubts as to your return; and, accordingly, doubt, certainly, as to my life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.945,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"672ae6d0676b45fdbf9a4c0a058a4d0858898097692768bebfad05404543500e","compact":"d5ca18eb86122785decf66fee6d9b8bc2e2cbd532af37c61a38e8d2fd30a0534","nasal":"3e6d76afe89652ed7656c2be5c014b980ab8d806975831e1129ebcc8246fa72c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":22,"english":"And the grief incident to my not seeing you shall burn me greatly, even, O monkey, as grief burn one that is already consumed by sorrow over and over again.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"96b8fa4036cf8f199cd4927f9ea23c50d41b4d752aff870e3aa09dbf1fcbe2c8","compact":"d27c0c0d4bfb0688c44b9dda113c6a0ccf5e4f32c06656c8691d5b014e256059","nasal":"6f413bf7da39677fd890838d8ecc19b981bbe6790eb14edfa92a016340a5d6a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":23,"english":"And, O hero, O lord of monkeys, this doubt is also before me. How, alas! shall the mighty lord of monkeys, albeit backed by the monkeys and bears, cross over the mighty main hard to cross, and (how shall) those forces consisting of bears and monkeys or those sons of the best of men (cross over the same)?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"87638d54c583c047d5ba94af88eef74a9cafed26499a8f7ead2369e35193bd99","compact":"49a567398638ab87154a49cf3fb9833be80bc44ffcc5f9246255f54b36c73b0a","nasal":"49a567398638ab87154a49cf3fb9833be80bc44ffcc5f9246255f54b36c73b0a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-24","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":24,"english":"And, O hero, O lord of monkeys, this doubt is also before me. How, alas! shall the mighty lord of monkeys, albeit backed by the monkeys and bears, cross over the mighty main hard to cross, and (how shall) those forces consisting of bears and monkeys or those sons of the best of men (cross over the same)?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.689,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6798144f0ae24f268c27c94d4c1cacfa8a608c8a5fac9e8fb864109b699bdf30","compact":"e3b71307c46096c6bf081c12242198c4059ed4a2c0105adec185a2e1ac835875","nasal":"7a384650cff20836d52e15999e31b6c3263ad8ef11a1f46ff59d9db858b5afae"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-25","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":25,"english":"In all the three worlds, Vinata's offspring, your self, and the Wind-god, have talone the power of crossing over the deep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037025","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c7d31c68cdc47b1132a1feeb2a1cec61892da7e1b5ccd8a5f7521e6ae3ea8f4","compact":"fdd8d639f8ee8bf84ef7428044fe21ff13972aa627e4f05502622f120e51e1b3","nasal":"2e8d329e901cf03c5de2f3407ab47fec88d4c13a733b50e194f9d5eb003621f3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-26","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":26,"english":"Then, for the accomplishment of this work, difficult to compass, what, O hero, O you best of those conversant with business, what way do you see as to its success?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037026","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f1fc5b50726d9655b570b3fc2741fc7c4d596a862f6863db2d62b6e6c8def18e","compact":"7b9e512072b6934908c9aa054a0d722b99085b3bc7d96b995ff5f1fe87f988d3","nasal":"7b9e512072b6934908c9aa054a0d722b99085b3bc7d96b995ff5f1fe87f988d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-27","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":27,"english":"Or you alone, O destroyer of hostile heroes, are quite enough for the fulfilment of this purpose; and you shall reap, in the shape of fame, the fruit of your achievement.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.895,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037027","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"75fffb948182f3016190f0ef8a3a3ac032de5988c8c843c95cc6dd95a4252644","compact":"cd74888932f76138d511273c705b21cdd9d821b82ec659626109ab7313edb004","nasal":"cd74888932f76138d511273c705b21cdd9d821b82ec659626109ab7313edb004"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-28","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":28,"english":"But if (Rāma) himself together with all his forces, conquering Ravana and (recovering me) in battle, returned victorious to his own city, this would be worthy of himself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.621,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037028","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78ee3b71728bcbf7bca9b771ddd8730a91bef71b3c13944ca8933c3e620cbd97","compact":"6ff9eb19c4e26ddf1e130a9a0036723ed06f59123f4c318d3e73fc4f75ddae29","nasal":"6ff9eb19c4e26ddf1e130a9a0036723ed06f59123f4c318d3e73fc4f75ddae29"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-29","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":29,"english":"If blocking up Lankā with his army, that afflictor of hostile hosts, Kākutstha took me (hence), that would be worthy of him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037029","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac4a6820ba4a29dab6259b1bb1a360459959985786b7c816f5f49b0d1082d286","compact":"e631be403f95bca9883d108b929fae4bea94de66f322a24c431bfc44ad429195","nasal":"7e9c44f59c13973ff4dcb05ea8b420e82e64331baa2e0f62cce514ef39153ea5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-30","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":30,"english":"Do you, therefore, adopt such means that the high-souled heroic warrior may have an opportunity of putting forth prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037030","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"88402311a5ec3960dd5e03f099bf6a7ecfc05a9e9fa59c53e06f06834837068e","compact":"eff1f0edfcdbdb32a5dab111960328a423cb375c6507437baa302a4807c557d6","nasal":"4c5b9c981b7ae6ab610c739ab51ea5c922f9ba48360184ff0c9b87047f228662"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-31","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":31,"english":"Hearing those words fraught with sense and reason and informed with affection, Hanumān, by way of reply said mildly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037031","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"886063121f0f14cfb9430223f3218b0abcf2a0150e28bf019d114a7f30332d9f","compact":"133621416cf1e66f222049f17fa4014ea28017c9e3d0cd95c3f7c64bfc02609a","nasal":"133621416cf1e66f222049f17fa4014ea28017c9e3d0cd95c3f7c64bfc02609a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-32","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":32,"english":"O revered lady, that foremost of monkeysthe lord of bears and monkeys-Sugrīva, possessed of truth, has made up his mind on your behalf.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.725,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037032","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de2483556f26ab5ae67a61a0597cda7f9546c623d7c0b5e18afe0fc57272c6b9","compact":"6680a904c71f698d961063c1d3f38fe77d26976a5d99ba241d1e3fc41a6be4e5","nasal":"35d60193d061501d9888ec5dfc906b705c0b4a252312ea9cc428451b5bb10e27"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-33","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":33,"english":"That destroyer of Rākşasas, O daughter of Vaidehi, environed by thousands of millions of monkeys, will come hither without delay.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037033","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"81eac9898e4d1c2f56f5d80b5ebeddc1fc609d9fd42ccf8d4528e31ce128cda6","compact":"d35007578cee51dca561203342e51369ac121107a5312c85326e4a0ce96bed3a","nasal":"d35007578cee51dca561203342e51369ac121107a5312c85326e4a0ce96bed3a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-34","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":34,"english":"And exceedingly powerful and mighty monkeys possessed of prowess, and speeding far with the rapidity of thought, are in his command. Nothing can impede their courses, either upward, or downward, or tending in both directions, and those ones of measureless energy never experience depression in the most arduous undertakings.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.639,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037034","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af9be438ca3e4f30f00aa984a4d94db86d7d7675e209e345c245999a750514cd","compact":"73799c4ccd573799191baf5f7e74ee41c5093ad18f41ded0360c4d83c4295062","nasal":"6bf703c60551fed1d7d5ffc7b7e0424ee3707045f0c14c3cc6db13f3a47e6a55"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-35","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":35,"english":"And exceedingly powerful and mighty monkeys possessed of prowess, and speeding far with the rapidity of thought, are in his command. Nothing can impede their courses, either upward, or downward, or tending in both directions, and those ones of measureless energy never experience depression in the most arduous undertakings.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037035","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b5362b578972e1c3e2a6b864133c538888b5f68800a817040c56a1abbdbd2d4","compact":"6698fab468cec1cc1ba18f517eaa121db8a1cb89daab76912dcc6d031ccf5426","nasal":"46aebe7bf949f1b713624c47cca942dde07d58483aca92b01898c3b0d61f6110"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-36","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":36,"english":"Braced by their exalted spirits, these, resorting to the aerial way have many a time and oft circumambulated the Earth containing mountains and meads.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037036","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d816b52a2ace046ec1ec8aa504765715b5f7dc25cefd66c7ba0d04b502990f70","compact":"42d9586e04fd88181e4c311dba9fec0ec3d52baf315e8dfb656b5b82070ab3a4","nasal":"42d9586e04fd88181e4c311dba9fec0ec3d52baf315e8dfb656b5b82070ab3a4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-37","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":37,"english":"There are (in that army) rangers of woods, some equal and some superior to me. And near Sugrīva there are none who are inferior to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037037","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af69a6b277982f8ebe075ab7cfab08461cc64d07e3f3ba4702b6d493a4c9f21f","compact":"6bef8cb41030c5a5de6903ec0cf3723a4223989507d87b795f55361b725c620f","nasal":"2178f3b3b9d73a1423d63b5659f32be21af8efb68dca3a8deb3c60257f91317a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-38","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":38,"english":"And since even I have reached this place, what shall I say of those ones endowed with immense might? Nor are superior (monkeys) sent on errands; it is only the inferior ones that are sent.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037038","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cc37171d12ffabca9a65ccf3b3a4b529d204d6398907dd7f830f8565a3443434","compact":"cc18c2261a0b8b50705b66b0a4f638de8f6e0cfebb3db13805d819bbf3f5e758","nasal":"8b01abc83cfe05d6f706bdcdc1fa7ed74d5e29fc2b61b8abe2189d8f1cedeb2c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-39","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":39,"english":"Then, O exalted one. you need not grieve: let your sorrow depart. Those leaders of monkey herds will come to Lankā by one bound; and, like to the risen Sun and Moon, those leonine men, having large numbers to back them, will come to your side, riding my back.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037039","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b32be5c255dbb09694820dc2890ab6b510ce24ea02d6ad6f2a4dfadac4859638","compact":"f0661e26a898045276727489ba8ab1dada9838084496765ec286093ef4ac5485","nasal":"891506b3c78439943fefd43e6dbc1b7b32b2f8172d4c070e80e05c5f7e1a44dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-40","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":40,"english":"Then, O exalted one. you need not grieve: let your sorrow depart. Those leaders of monkey herds will come to Lankā by one bound; and, like to the risen Sun and Moon, those leonine men, having large numbers to back them, will come to your side, riding my back.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037040","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5c9a9901202161f14aee50ba34374fdc1d2143892d015ffc0b6cc9ad2b974eb","compact":"96975540868b2a2ac22d88428888f92e3635a352bc7e32aba33249cf2d65ea8c","nasal":"c3da1c0af8198039d0180645335169c7c88e0f79c17f16a44c7fc001c281caed"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-41","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":41,"english":"Those heroes and foremost of men, Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa both, coming to the city of Lankā, shall destroy her by means of their shafts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037041","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1a2011757c499ffe3891506751a66945a3c3d978795ae52ed7c175a552603d5f","compact":"a11219d3155d7eb428a0595320fa25263590d29439ef2a09bab1bf5da6c92175","nasal":"10e76038ab35fae308f6ce818c9a748c5af7fd69b6714a3e7816c87d1fb3335f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-42","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":42,"english":"And slaying Rāvaņa together with his adherents, Raghu's son, taking you, O paragon among women, shall return to his own city.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037042","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"581aa935da7896d1edbbb1ba26e3976ae13fba281ebd8748ec38550486f2ae3a","compact":"fe3e6261c265a5eec2946b1609795cf74e7357531a8e2d402204a4151ddb7179","nasal":"382721b217d13e2796ce8414e5883c14e1bff25857c36994eaa419abf0d85cca"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-43","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":43,"english":"Therefore, do you take heart, good betide you! Do you remain, eagerly wishing for the time. It will not be long before you shall behold Rāma resembling flaming fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.696,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037043","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0114d0a250e7cd133fb7d5067a55d6113b770ddcda21411b2fceeff7abc819fc","compact":"f2fecef44f112a180383398dcae9c5d533d70fb206446652621f3e520d1ab5c6","nasal":"3bb6498af5c760eddc2a539ff7d3f3a3489caad819f0ae584e6df3d1ebe2485a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-37-44","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":37,"verse":44,"english":"On the lord of Rākṣasas being slain along with his counsellors and friends, you shall meet with Rāma, even as Rohinī meet with the Moon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-39-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5037044","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e14e10176265830bdf4b4fc